<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill falls to 6.98 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill falls to 6.98 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it raised the cut-off price at its weeekly auction of 91-day treasury bills to 98.29 rupees from 98.28 rupees.</p>
<p>The yield fell to 6.98 percent from 7.02 percent, dealers said.</p>
